.TH GENEEXPRESSION 1 2000-1月 "limma_impactsort" "limma_impactsort"
.SH NAME
limma_impactsort \- make the impact sort of the limma differential expression analysis result
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIlimma_impactsort(\fBx\fR as any, 
\fBtop\fR as integer = 2147483647, 
\fBlogfc_impact\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBclass\fR as list = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBnames\fR as list = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
make the impact sort of the limma differential expression analysis result
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- 
 the limma result data, which can be a vector of the 
 @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.DataFrame.LimmaTable\fR object, a pipeline object of the limma result, or 
 a tuple list of the multiple limma result groups(the slot value of the list 
 is the limma result of one group).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtop\fB \fR\- 
 take the top n genes of the impact sort result, by default is all of the 
 genes in the input data.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlogfc_impact\fB \fR\- 
 evaluate the impact value of each gene based on the log2 fold change value 
 or based on the p-value?
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBclass\fB \fR\- 
 the id class data, example as: 
 list(class1 = c(...), class2 = c(...), class3 = c(...))
 
 this parameter can also be provided in the format of 
 \fBlist(id1 = "class1", id2 = "class2", ...)\fR, i.e. each id is mapped to 
 its class label directly.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBnames\fB \fR\- should be a list of id mapping to name. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a vector of the @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.GCModeller.Workbench.ExperimentDesigner.ImpactResult\fR data object that is sorted by 
 the impact value in descending order: the \fBtotal\fR impact value of each 
 gene across all of the input limma result groups, the \fBmax\fR impact value 
 and the corresponding \fBtop_group\fR, and the class label and the name of 
 each gene if the \fBclass\fR/\fBnames\fR parameter is provided;
 
 this function returns a R# error message object if the input data can not 
 be cast to a collection of the @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.DataFrame.LimmaTable\fR data.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneExpression
.SH FILES
.PP
phenotype_kit.dll
.PP
